# The provided files must arrive byte-identical on every machine.
#
# Git's default on Windows converts LF to CRLF on checkout. That leaves the content
# unchanged but the BYTES different, which breaks two things: the sha256 values
# analysis/findings.json records for provenance, and the exercise's instruction that
# the provided data is not to be modified. Marking them -text switches the
# conversion off, so what we were given is what every reviewer gets.
data/*.csv -text
model/*.pkl -text binary

# Everything else can follow the platform's convention.
* text=auto
